- Teleport to (110,110) to escape; wait 1s, check escapeTimer decreased? Actually police may be far. Then set escapeTimer=0.5 and wait 1.2s; check stage complete.
- Wait 3.6s; check currentHeist 1, stage approach, jobComplete hidden.
- Teleport to heist 2 marker (7.4,22), press E; check stage combat, guards 3. Screenshot.
- Maybe use debug to kill guards? We can set guards health to 0.1 and fire once at one; but damageGuard not exposed. Could just check combat. Then reset? For final screenshot, maybe not needed.
- Mobile page: 390x844, click start, wait, screenshot. Check touch controls display and buttons bounding boxes within viewport. Also simulate joystick pointerdown/move and check game.touchMove; action button etc.
- Check no console errors.

We need to be careful that moving forward W may start? No, only E starts. Player at -90.5, moving east 0.8s at speed ~? Player speed walk 4.2? distance 3m -> x -87.5, still 3.7m from marker. Prompt remains. Press E starts. Good.

Let's write the script. For aiming, use projection and iterate. We'll take screenshots after heist start and after loot/escape.

Aiming function in Node:
```
async function aimAtGuard() {
  for (let i=0;i<8;i++) {
    const ndc = await page.evaluate(() => {
      const { guards, camera, THREE } = window.__SUNSET__;
      const g = guards.find(g=>g.alive);
      if (!g) return null;
      const v = new THREE.Vector3(g.x, 1.25, g.z).project(camera);
      return {x:v.x, y:v.y};
    });
    if (!ndc) return false;
    if (Math.abs(ndc.x) < 0.02 && Math.abs(ndc.y) < 0.03) return true;
    await page.evaluate(({dx,dy}) => {
      const { cam } = window.__SUNSET__;
      cam.yaw -= dx * 0.25; // need sign
      cam.pitch -= dy * 0.08;
    }, {dx: ndc.x, dy: ndc.y});
    await page.waitForTimeout(120);
  }
  return false;
}
```
Need to verify sign. NDC x positive if guard is right of center. To turn right, decrease yaw (as derived). So `cam.yaw -= dx * 0.25` yes. But the camera is over-shoulder and yaw affects camera position; if guard right, decreasing yaw rotates view right. Good. For NDC y positive (guard above center), need look up => decrease pitch. So `cam.pitch -= dy * 0.08`. But decreasing pitch also lowers camera height, which might move guard down; convergence maybe. Try.

But note: `camera` projection uses the camera's current matrixWorld, updated each frame. After setting cam.yaw, wait 120ms. Good.

